  "answer": "A \"Copy as plain text\" shortcut (for example Ctrl+Shift+C) has been requested before in PowerToys#25192 and PowerToys#21001. In #25192 the maintainer said they had considered it, but earlier feedback was that people want plain text either on demand or always. #21001 was closed as a duplicate of the older tracking issue #1684, which wasn't in the retrieved tickets, so follow that issue and add your use case there. No one has shipped this feature yet. Until then, the workaround from those tickets is to paste the text into a plain editor like Notepad, copy it again, and paste it into the target app. Your LibreOffice case, where PowerToys' plain-text paste still keeps the source's plain-text styling, isn't covered in those tickets. Using LibreOffice's own paste-unformatted command, as you already do, is the best option for now."
 },
